{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1126","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1126","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1126\",\"parent_revision\":\"6ac3a5c9aad6a08c8df82419e5976e52d0cc57bbf966148fcdab5d05693c7b27\",\"root_revision\":\"6ac3a5c9aad6a08c8df82419e5976e52d0cc57bbf966148fcdab5d05693c7b27\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/plugin-creator/tests/test_frontmatter_validator.py` has no test verifying that running `fix()` twice on an already-fixed file produces no further changes. A non-idempotent fix causes the \\\"stashed changes conflicted\\\" symptom in prek pre-commit runs (this failure mode is already documented in `test_auto_sync_manifests.py`).\\n\\nAlso: `test_frontmatter_fixes.py` TestFM009Guard parametrized cases assert specific line strings appear in `fixed_text` but do not assert the result is valid YAML \u2014 a fix producing syntactically broken YAML would pass.\\n\\nSuggested tests:\\n- `test_fix_when_applied_twice_then_second_call_produces_no_changes`\\n- Add `ruamel.yaml` parse assertion to `TestFM009Guard` parametrized body\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **add frontmattervalidator fix-idempotency tests** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Test quality audit 2026-03-29\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"24af52f947508fd7b9f92a33423011ef8ca8f69f222242b83e01825b01f37d4f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWShUA\"}"}